 r←UrlScheme url;ind;scheme
⍝ Returns the scheme of `url` - 'https', 'mailto', 'javascript' and so on - or '' when there
⍝ is none.
⍝ A colon on its own does not make a scheme: in "docs/a:b" it belongs to the path, so a
⍝ slash before the colon rules it out. Nor does anything but a letter, a digit and "+-.".
 r←''
 ind←url⍳':'
 :If ind≤≢url
 :AndIf ~∨/'/'=(ind-1)↑url
     scheme←(ind-1)↑url
     :If 0<≢scheme
     :AndIf ∧/scheme∊⎕A,(⎕C ⎕A),⎕D,'+-.'
         r←scheme
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
